From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 23:40:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] vulkan/wsi/x11: a new surface starts with no doubled window

Patch 0041 gave the X11 surface three fields for a window the compositor makes
two views wide (doubled, doubled_seen, view_width) and set them only when such a
swapchain is made; wsi_CreateXcbSurfaceKHR and wsi_CreateXlibSurfaceKHR allocate
the surface with vk_alloc2, which does not clear it. x11_surface_get_capabilities
halves the extents whenever doubled and doubled_seen read as true, so a window's
surface reported half its width whenever the allocation held old bytes there: on
any X server, for every Mesa Vulkan driver, a stereo swapchain or not. "With
Xcb, minImageExtent, maxImageExtent, and currentExtent must always equal the
window size" (VK_KHR_xcb_surface; the same for Xlib). A stereo swapchain made at
that size is never told it is out of date (the suboptimal check is skipped for a
stereo chain), so its program drew each eye at half the window's width for good:
the Dolphin emulator on Vulkan, 4 of 10 and 4 of 8 fresh sessions (ORDER 39).
Both create functions now set the three fields.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
--- a/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common_x11.c
+++ b/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common_x11.c
@@ -1110,6 +1110,9 @@
    surface->has_alpha = visual_has_alpha(visual, visual_depth);
    surface->stereo_swapchain_created = false;
    surface->stereo_chain = NULL;
+   surface->doubled = false;
+   surface->doubled_seen = false;
+   surface->view_width = 0;
 
    *pSurface = VkIcdSurfaceBase_to_handle(&surface->xcb.base);
    return VK_SUCCESS;
@@ -1144,6 +1147,9 @@
    surface->has_alpha = visual_has_alpha(visual, visual_depth);
    surface->stereo_swapchain_created = false;
    surface->stereo_chain = NULL;
+   surface->doubled = false;
+   surface->doubled_seen = false;
+   surface->view_width = 0;
 
    *pSurface = VkIcdSurfaceBase_to_handle(&surface->xlib.base);
    return VK_SUCCESS;
